@startuml mo_house
title mo_house: MO House XML + roll-call PDFs
start
:for each year in the lookback window (MOGOV_LOOKBACK_YEARS)
and session type 1-4: GET documents.house.mo.gov/xml/<YY><t>.zip;
if (body is a zip?) then (yes)
  :read every *.xml in the archive;
elseif (regular session of the current year?) then (yes)
  :open session (no zip yet):
  walk MemberList / BillList / SenateActList
  and fetch each linked per-member / per-bill XML;
else (HTML page)
  :skip: no such session
  (site answers unknown codes with 200 + HTML);
endif
if (session owned by this shard?) then (yes)
  :gzip each XML file, unchanged, under RAW_DIR/mo_house_xml/SESSION/;
  :one state row per file in mo_house_xml_files
  (path, URL, size, sha256, fetched_at);
endif
:parse each file once with lxml (every shard)
and collect its RollCallPDF URLs;
:Parser (mogov.parsers.mo_house) reads this shard's gzip files
and walks each document: bills with actions, sponsors, texts,
amendments, roll calls, subjects and hearings; members with
committee posts; sessions, committees and list items;
:typed rows land as the mo_house_xml tables;
:owned roll-call PDFs -> pdfplumber layout text
-> header fields + one row per (roll call, member token);
note right
  Tokens are printed surnames ("SMITH 46", "MR SPEAKER"),
  matched to members in dbt (int_mo_house__member_identity).
  PDFs are cached forever: roll calls never change.
end note
:mo_house_rollcalls, mo_house_rollcall_votes;
stop
@enduml
